WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.201 --> 00:00:02.234
-Welcome back
to "The Tonight Show."

00:00:02.234 --> 00:00:03.236
We're about to play
"Hey, Robot"!

00:00:03.236 --> 00:00:06.372
-♪ Hey, hey, hey, robot ♪

00:00:06.372 --> 00:00:07.806
♪ Hey, robot ♪

00:00:07.806 --> 00:00:09.175
-To play against a robot,

00:00:09.175 --> 00:00:11.477
I'm going to need some help
from someone smart.

00:00:11.477 --> 00:00:13.679
He's a very funny comedian
and the host

00:00:13.679 --> 00:00:16.916
of the multiple Emmy-winning
show "Last Week Tonight,"

00:00:16.916 --> 00:00:19.986
which airs Sundays
at 11:00 pm on HBO.

00:00:19.986 --> 00:00:22.288
Please welcome John Oliver.

00:00:22.288 --> 00:00:23.289
[ Clapping ]
That's what I'm talking about.

00:00:23.289 --> 00:00:24.691
-Hello, there.
-Here we go.

00:00:24.691 --> 00:00:25.992
Look at you.
-Hello, Jimmy.

00:00:25.992 --> 00:00:27.493
Hello, everybody.

00:00:27.493 --> 00:00:30.330
-It's so good to see you.

00:00:30.330 --> 00:00:31.331
This is bizarre.

00:00:31.331 --> 00:00:32.631
It's like you're

00:00:32.631 --> 00:00:34.200
Max Headroom or something.

00:00:34.200 --> 00:00:37.136
[ Laughter ]
This is like an art piece.

00:00:37.136 --> 00:00:39.138
[ Clapping ]
I like it. Yeah, it's cool.

00:00:39.138 --> 00:00:41.875
Now, John, this is based

00:00:41.875 --> 00:00:44.310
on a real board game,
called Hey Robot,

00:00:44.310 --> 00:00:46.245
that you can play at home,
everyone watching.

00:00:46.245 --> 00:00:47.981
It's like the classic game
Password,

00:00:47.981 --> 00:00:50.549
but your partner is
a smart speaker.

00:00:50.549 --> 00:00:53.753
First, what I will do is I will
pick a card with a word on it

00:00:53.753 --> 00:00:56.322
and we'll take turns asking
a question to get the speaker

00:00:56.322 --> 00:00:58.424
to say that word somewhere
in its answer.

00:00:58.424 --> 00:01:00.627
You ready for this?
I will go first.

00:01:00.627 --> 00:01:02.695
-Yeah, I'm ready.
-Okay, bud.

00:01:02.695 --> 00:01:06.833
Okay, so I have to get it
to say leprechaun.

00:01:06.833 --> 00:01:08.134 line:0%
-Okay.

00:01:08.134 --> 00:01:09.735 line:0%
-Now, if I don't get it,
then you go.

00:01:09.735 --> 00:01:12.405 line:0%
You try to give it a shot.
Alright, here we go.

00:01:12.405 --> 00:01:14.040 line:0%
Oh, my God.

00:01:14.040 --> 00:01:17.510 line:0%
Alexa, what fictional
cartoon character

00:01:17.510 --> 00:01:21.614 line:0%
is associated
with the pot of gold?

00:01:21.614 --> 00:01:24.016 line:0%
[ Laughing ]

00:01:24.016 --> 00:01:26.252 line:0%
-Here's something I found
on the Web.

00:01:26.252 --> 00:01:28.921 line:0%
According to grumpycats.com,

00:01:28.921 --> 00:01:31.424 line:0%
cartoon Grumpy Cat frowns next
to four shamrocks

00:01:31.424 --> 00:01:33.526 line:0%
with "pot of gold"
and "I hope it's empty"

00:01:33.526 --> 00:01:36.695 line:0%
printed around her
on a cute green shirt.

00:01:36.695 --> 00:01:38.765 line:0%
[ Buzzer ]
-That makes zero sense.

00:01:38.765 --> 00:01:40.866 line:0%
-For a start, there,
Alexa has got to spend less time

00:01:40.866 --> 00:01:42.068 line:0%
on grumpycat.com.

00:01:42.068 --> 00:01:44.070 line:0%
If that's where she's
getting all her news,

00:01:44.070 --> 00:01:45.204 line:0%
[ Laughter ]
we're in real trouble.

00:01:45.204 --> 00:01:48.007 line:0%
-[ Clapping ]

00:01:48.007 --> 00:01:50.209 line:0%
-At best, it's an aggregation
site, Alexa.

00:01:50.209 --> 00:01:53.279 line:0%
You cannot trust any of the data
that's coming out of that.

00:01:53.279 --> 00:01:54.447 line:0%
-Okay, here we go.

00:01:54.447 --> 00:01:56.382 line:0%
John, you have to try to see
if you can get it

00:01:56.382 --> 00:01:58.451 line:0%
to say this word.
-Okay.

00:02:00.052 --> 00:02:02.822 line:0%
